Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-01-2000||04:12 AM||||When im sitting in traffic and is ......lets say about 80 or so out....My temp gauge reads about 220 or so. I drove on the e-way today at about 95 to 110mph for about a hour and my temp was at 210 when I stoped. My problem is that I have never seen or heard my fan go on.Is it possable that ive been running without my fan working?? I even changed the thermostat (195) and its the same. The old one was all nasty looking.<P><BR>P.S. When I let the car sit and run it will go over 220deg. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||08-01-2000||08:14 AM||||I believe the fan thermostatic switch does not turn on the fan until it reaches around 235 degrees F.  The fan is supposed to come on when you turn the A/C switch to any function that would normally run the A/C compressor such as Max, Bi-level, and Defrost.||||reg||1
